---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/legal-layout.astro";
import { ROUTES } from "@/constants/routes";
import { SITE } from "@/constants/site";
---

<LegalLayout
  id="terms"
  heading="Terms of service"
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms for using shadcn-labs.com and buying a Shadcn Labs sponsorship through GitHub Sponsors or Dodo Payments."
  updated="Nov 01, 2026"
>
  <p>
    These terms cover your use of shadcn-labs.com and any sponsorship you buy
    from Shadcn Labs ("we", "us"), operated by {SITE.AUTHOR.NAME}. By using the
    site or subscribing to a sponsorship tier, you agree to them.
  </p>

  <h3>Open-source projects</h3>
  <p>
    Our registries, templates, and ports are free and open source. Each project
    is governed by the license in its own repository, not by these terms, and is
    provided "as is" without warranty.
  </p>

  <h3>Sponsorships</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Each tier is a monthly subscription billed in advance, in US dollars, at
      the price shown on the <a class="link-underline" href={ROUTES.SPONSORS}>sponsors page</a> or
      on the GitHub Sponsors tier page you check out from. It renews every month
      until you cancel.
    </li>
    <li>
      The perks for each tier are listed on the sponsors page and in the matching
      GitHub Sponsors tier. If the two descriptions differ, the tier description
      shown by the provider at checkout governs.
    </li>
    <li>
      We deliver placements as soon as we have your logo, link, and name,
      usually within a few business days of payment. Send them through the
      welcome-message instructions or the <a
        class="link-underline"
        href={`${ROUTES.CONTACT}?inquiry=sponsorship`}>sponsorship contact form</a
      >.
    </li>
    <li>
      Placement order within a tier, logo size, and layout are at our
      discretion and may change as the sites change.
    </li>
    <li>
      Where we place your logo on our own sites, the link to your website is
      do-follow. Links inside GitHub READMEs and other GitHub-hosted pages follow
      GitHub's own rules.
    </li>
    <li>
      We may change tier prices or perks for future billing periods. We will
      tell active sponsors by email before a change applies to them.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>GitHub Sponsors</h3>
  <p>
    GitHub Sponsors is our primary checkout. GitHub processes your payment,
    handles receipts, and appears on your statement. Your sponsorship is also
    subject to <a
      class="link-underline"
      href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/github-terms/github-sponsors-additional-terms"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener">GitHub's sponsor terms</a
    >. Change your amount or cancel at any time from your GitHub account;
    GitHub confirms the change to us. GitHub decides whether a GitHub payment is
    refundable, and any refund is issued by GitHub.
  </p>

  <h3>Dodo Payments</h3>
  <p>
    If GitHub is not an option for your team, you can pay the same tiers through
    <a
      class="link-underline"
      href="https://dodopayments.com"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener">Dodo Payments</a
    >, our merchant of record. Dodo Payments processes your payment, collects
    applicable sales tax or VAT, issues your invoices, and appears on your
    statement. Your purchase is also subject to Dodo Payments' own terms. We
    never see or store your full card details. Dodo sponsors can update payment
    methods, download invoices, or cancel from the Dodo customer portal linked in
    their subscription emails.
  </p>

  <h3>Refunds</h3>
  <p>
    Refunds follow the provider that took your payment. GitHub payments are
    refunded, if at all, by GitHub under GitHub's policy. Dodo Payments refunds
    follow our <a class="link-underline" href={ROUTES.REFUNDS}>refund policy</a>.
    Cancelling stops future renewals; placements stay live until the end of the
    period you already paid for.
  </p>

  <h3>Your content</h3>
  <p>
    You confirm that you have the right to use the logo, name, and link you send
    us, and you allow us to display them across our sites, repositories, and
    social posts for the length of your sponsorship. We may decline or remove
    any sponsor or content that is illegal, misleading, malicious, or harmful to
    our community.
  </p>

  <h3>Acceptable use</h3>
  <p>
    Do not attempt to disrupt the site, abuse the contact form, or access data
    you are not entitled to.
  </p>

  <h3>Liability</h3>
  <p>
    The site and sponsorships are provided "as is". We do not guarantee any
    specific traffic, clicks, or conversions; audience analytics show past
    traffic only. To the extent the law allows, our total liability for any
    claim related to a sponsorship is limited to the amount you paid for it in
    the three months before the claim.
  </p>

  <h3>Changes</h3>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. The date at the top shows the latest version;
    continuing to use the site or keeping an active sponsorship after a change
    means you accept it.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
